# The shortcut's store: readings come back as Readings, but outages come back as the lines they are kept as, and a
# summary is kept and given back as a line; the Outage that `save_outage` puts no get gives back, and no Summary type
# exists. `summary` returns the kept line when there is one (`return` in the `if let`), else reads the day's readings and
# writes the new line: the code after the early return is the other arm of that choice. A library's operation whose
# result the body names (`read_to_string`, `split`, `find`, `collect`, `fold`, the `next()`s a tuple binds), or that
# changes the String it runs on (`push_str`), is a step; what it touches stays its caller's. Each file is read, used and
# written by the route: it stands on both sides.
#
# Issues marked: #126 what the own arrow keeps; #138 an error a step hands on.

route harvest.ReadingStore
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.new
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.new/ReadingStore() # the struct built by its literal
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save/push_str   # push_str changes the String
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/split
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/next
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/next#2
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/next#3
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.history/Reading()
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save_outage
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save_outage/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.save_outage/push_str   # push_str changes the String
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.outages
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.outages/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/find   # `if let Some(line)` names what find gives
choice ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1   # the code after `return` is the other arm
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/read_to_string
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/split
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/next   # drawn in the arm the early return makes
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/next#2   # drawn in the arm the early return makes
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/next#3   # drawn in the arm the early return makes
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/ReadingStore.history/Reading()
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/collect
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/fold
step ReadingStore()/ReadingStore.summary/?1/fold#2

